The architecture tells us what the target model is. The core capability view tells us what the bank actually needs to shape or build to make that model real.

These capabilities are not all separate products. They are the reusable building blocks and control points the bank needs across multiple use cases.

The value of this slide is that it shifts the conversation from abstract architecture into enterprise capability priorities.”

